course: dictionary
lesson: 5789
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and mac is one of them. You cannot tell which meaning is meant by looking at the word alone. Read the words around it, because the context tells you which meaning fits.
explain: «Take your mac, it's raining.» Here a mac is a raincoat, short for mackintosh. The word raining is the clue, because you wear a raincoat when it rains.
explain: «Macs can get viruses and other harmful software; they are just attacked less often than Windows computers.» Here Mac means an Apple computer. Software, viruses and Windows are all computer words, so they point to the computer meaning.
explain: Mac at the start of a name, as in MacDonald, means «son of» in Scottish and Irish names. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it makes sense.
fact: Mac can mean a raincoat, an Apple computer, or part of a Scottish or Irish name.
fact: A mac is a raincoat, short for mackintosh.
fact: A Mac is an Apple Macintosh computer.
fact: In informal US speech, «Mac» is a way of speaking to a man whose name you don't know, like «buddy».
fact: Mac (or Mc) at the start of a name means «son of», as in MacDonald. Mac and cheese is macaroni pasta in cheese sauce.
exercise: «Take your mac, it's raining.» What is a mac in this sentence? | A sort of cup | A cold drink | A bus stop | *A raincoat, to keep you dry
exercise: «Autosave means the program saves for you every few minutes; Ctrl+S, or Cmd+S on a Mac, saves by hand.» In this sentence, what is a Mac? | *An Apple computer | A man's name | A raincoat | A dish of pasta
exercise: In Scottish names, what does «Mac» at the start mean? | A computer | Very hungry | *Son of | A raincoat
test: «Macs can get viruses and other harmful software; they are just attacked less often than Windows computers.» What does Macs mean here? | Raincoats | Scottish sons | *Apple computers | Pasta dishes
test: Which word in this sentence tells you that Macs are computers? | Other | *Software | Less | Often
exam: A man in a shop says, «What can I do for you, mac?» What does mac mean? | *A way of speaking to a man whose name you don't know | A computer | A dish of pasta | A raincoat
